WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.024 --> 00:00:19.568
was early on the morning of January nineteenth when Bessie found me up and nearly dressed.

2
00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:25.033
I was going to school that day on a coach that passed Gateshead at six o'clock.

3
00:00:26.174 --> 00:00:30.297
Bessie tried to get me to eat some breakfast, but I was too excited.

4
00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:35.697
As we left the nursery, Bessie said, "Will you say good-bye to Mrs.

5
00:00:35.757 --> 00:00:37.498
Reed?" "No.

6
00:00:38.019 --> 00:00:41.661
She came to my bed last night and told me not to disturb her this morning.

7
00:00:42.782 --> 00:00:46.184
She also said to remember that she'd always been my best friend."

8
00:00:46.204 --> 00:00:48.366
"And what did you say?"

9
00:00:48.386 --> 00:00:52.568
"Nothing. I turned my face to the wall."

10
00:00:53.749 --> 00:00:55.731
Bessie scolded me but I didn't care.

11
00:00:57.051 --> 00:00:59.033
I was leaving Gateshead forever!

12
00:01:00.174 --> 00:01:05.196
Carrying a lantern, she walked me down to the porter's lodge, where my trunk had been sent the

13
00:01:05.236 --> 00:01:05.857
night before.

14
00:01:07.057 --> 00:01:11.718
When the coach arrived, my trunk was hoisted up, and I was placed on a seat.

15
00:01:13.599 --> 00:01:15.939
I remembered little of the fifty-mile journey.

16
00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:23.101
The afternoon was wet and misty; as darkness fell, we left the towns behind and moved out into

17
00:01:23.222 --> 00:01:23.962
open country.

18
00:01:25.102 --> 00:01:28.083
I was lulled to sleep by the wind rushing through the trees.

19
00:01:29.343 --> 00:01:31.804
I woke up when we arrived at Lowood school.

20
00:01:32.924 --> 00:01:38.085
A servant led me through a door in a high wall, and then into a large building with

21
00:01:38.185 --> 00:01:39.006
many windows.

22
00:01:40.186 --> 00:01:43.347
We entered a room with a fire, where she left me alone.

23
00:01:44.607 --> 00:01:47.128
A few minutes later, two women entered.

24
00:01:47.148 --> 00:01:53.450
"This child is very young to have been sent alone," said the first woman, whose name was Miss

25
00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:57.371
Temple. She was tall with dark hair and eyes.

26
00:01:57.391 --> 00:01:59.351
"Are you tired?"

27
00:01:59.731 --> 00:02:02.312
she asked, placing her hand on my shoulder.

28
00:02:03.464 --> 00:02:05.185
"A little, ma'am," I admitted.

29
00:02:05.205 --> 00:02:07.647
"And hungry, too, no doubt.

30
00:02:08.708 --> 00:02:11.550
Let her have some supper before she goes to bed, Miss Miller."

31
00:02:13.291 --> 00:02:17.574
Then Miss Temple asked me about my family and whether I could read or write.

32
00:02:18.735 --> 00:02:20.416
She touched my cheek gently.

33
00:02:20.436 --> 00:02:23.178
"I hope you'll be a good girl.

34
00:02:24.219 --> 00:02:25.660
Now run along with Miss Miller."

35
00:02:26.772 --> 00:02:31.973
Miss Miller, one of the teachers, led me through a maze of corridors until we came to a

36
00:02:32.093 --> 00:02:35.714
huge room filled with girls in brown dresses and pinafores.

37
00:02:36.915 --> 00:02:43.717
Seated at long tables and bent over their studies, they appeared countless, though I later learned there were

38
00:02:43.937 --> 00:02:45.417
eighty students at the school.

39
00:02:46.597 --> 00:02:51.359
A supper of oat cake and water was soon served, but I was too tired to eat.

40
00:02:52.499 --> 00:02:56.220
The next morning we all sat down to breakfast in the dining hall.

41
00:02:56.796 --> 00:02:59.918
A noxious smell came from the basins on the tables.

42
00:02:59.939 --> 00:03:04.002
"Disgusting!" said one of the older girls.

43
00:03:04.022 --> 00:03:06.784
"The porridge is burned again."

44
00:03:08.025 --> 00:03:12.748
I tried a mouthful, but burned porridge is almost as bad as rotten potatoes.

45
00:03:14.669 --> 00:03:17.432
Breakfast was over and no one had eaten.

46
00:03:18.632 --> 00:03:23.116
We filed into the schoolroom and at nine o'clock sat down to our lessons.

47
00:03:24.372 --> 00:03:27.674
There were four classes, and I was placed in the lowest.

48
00:03:28.915 --> 00:03:32.116
Suddenly everyone rose as Miss Temple entered the room.

49
00:03:33.277 --> 00:03:38.880
Taking her seat near a globe, Miss Temple began giving a geography lesson to the older girls.

50
00:03:40.081 --> 00:03:45.323
The other teachers led classes in history and grammar followed by writing and arithmetic.

51
00:03:46.504 --> 00:03:49.766
At last the clock struck twelve, and Miss Temple stood up.

52
00:03:49.786 --> 00:03:54.493
"This morning you had a breakfast that you couldn't eat," she said.

53
00:03:54.513 --> 00:03:59.097
"I've ordered a snack of bread and cheese to be served to all."

54
00:04:00.178 --> 00:04:03.360
The girls cheered while the teachers looked at her in surprise.

55
00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:07.364
"I'll take responsibility for this," she said.

56
00:04:08.545 --> 00:04:12.128
The bread and cheese were brought in, to the delight of the whole school.

57
00:04:14.049 --> 00:04:16.792
Then the order "To the garden" was given.

58
00:04:17.973 --> 00:04:21.436
Each student put on a coarse straw bonnet and a gray cloak.

59
00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.261
I followed the girls outdoors.

60
00:04:25.581 --> 00:04:31.282
The garden was a wide space, surrounded by walls so high that they shut out any view.

61
00:04:32.503 --> 00:04:34.923
A covered veranda ran down one side.

62
00:04:36.124 --> 00:04:39.545
It was a cold, drizzly day for outdoor exercise.

63
00:04:40.825 --> 00:04:44.926
I had not spoken to anyone yet, nor had anyone noticed me.

64
00:04:46.146 --> 00:04:47.887
But I was used to being lonely.

65
00:04:49.087 --> 00:04:54.590
I leaned against a pillar of the verandah and tried to forget both the cold and my hunger.

66
00:04:55.691 --> 00:05:01.475
Presently I noticed a stone tablet over the door that said "Lowood Institution."

67
00:05:02.676 --> 00:05:08.880
I was still pondering the meaning of the word "institution" when the sound of a hollow cough caught

68
00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:09.600
my attention.

69
00:05:10.821 --> 00:05:14.684
I saw a girl of about 14, sitting on a stone bench.

70
00:05:16.665 --> 00:05:20.688
She was bent over a book; turning a page, she happened to look up.

71
00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:23.121
"Is your book interesting?"

72
00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:24.001
I asked.

73
00:05:25.222 --> 00:05:27.463
She paused for a second and examined me.

74
00:05:27.483 --> 00:05:29.104
"I like it."

75
00:05:29.124 --> 00:05:30.845
"What's it about?"

76
00:05:30.865 --> 00:05:32.906
"You may look at it."

77
00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:35.187
She offered me the book.

78
00:05:36.488 --> 00:05:41.470
I'd hoped that the book would contain fairy tales, but there was nothing like that on its densely

79
00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:42.351
printed pages.

80
00:05:43.632 --> 00:05:47.854
I returned it, and she was about to start reading again when I interrupted her.

81
00:05:47.874 --> 00:05:51.656
"Why is this place called an institution?"

82
00:05:52.916 --> 00:05:55.778
"We're all charity children," the girl explained.

83
00:05:55.798 --> 00:06:02.783
"Everyone has lost one or both parents, and this is an institution for educating orphans.

84
00:06:04.024 --> 00:06:08.728
We, or our friends, pay fifteen pounds a year so that we can stay here."

85
00:06:10.609 --> 00:06:11.510
I was still puzzled.

86
00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:14.972
"Then why do they call us charity children?"

87
00:06:14.992 --> 00:06:19.936
"Because fifteen pounds isn't enough to cover the cost of our living here.

88
00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:24.303
The rest is made up by subscriptions from benevolent people."

89
00:06:25.504 --> 00:06:28.526
I asked more questions, and the girl explained that Mr.

90
00:06:28.586 --> 00:06:31.849
Brocklehurst was the treasurer and manager of Lowood.

91
00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:37.574
A clergyman, he lived in a fine, large house two miles away.

92
00:06:37.594 --> 00:06:41.377
"So the school doesn't belong to Miss Temple?"

93
00:06:41.737 --> 00:06:42.238
I asked.

94
00:06:42.258 --> 00:06:44.259
"I wish it did!

95
00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:46.801
She has to answer to Mr.

96
00:06:46.821 --> 00:06:49.724
Brocklehurst for everything she does as superintendent.

97
00:06:50.868 --> 00:06:52.750
He buys all our clothes and food."

98
00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:54.891
"Are you happy here?"

99
00:06:54.911 --> 00:06:57.413
"You ask too many questions.

100
00:06:58.534 --> 00:06:59.335
I want to read."

101
00:07:01.076 --> 00:07:05.160
But I asked one more and learned that her name was Helen Burns.

102
00:07:06.421 --> 00:07:09.683
Just then the bell sounded for lunch, so we filed inside.

103
00:07:10.844 --> 00:07:15.448
The odor that filled the dining hall was scarcely more appetizing than at breakfast.

104
00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:19.792
I could eat little of the fatty meat and gray potatoes.

105
00:07:21.112 --> 00:07:25.595
After lunch we adjourned to the schoolroom, where lessons continued until five o'clock.

106
00:07:26.775 --> 00:07:34.360
During the afternoon Miss Scatcherd, one of the teachers, dismissed Helen in disgrace from history class and forced

107
00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.501
her to stand in the middle of the schoolroom.

108
00:07:37.762 --> 00:07:42.624
It seemed a terrible punishment to me, but Helen neither wept nor blushed.

109
00:07:43.805 --> 00:07:48.388
And I was left to wonder whether she was a good or naughty child.
